<p>Phase 4 represents the long-range vision for SR-177 north of West Haven into Box Elder County. As of September 27, 2026, UDOT has not announced a formal environmental study for this segment or published an alignment. A locally preserved corridor has existed since a 2009 study, and 2026 Weber County records show an unresolved question about where the corridor should run.{% cite "weber-north-legacy-2009-study" %}{% cite "wc-pc-joint-minutes-mar2026" %}</p>

<hr class="divider">

<div class="section-label">Route Options Map</div>
<h2>Where the Corridor Has Been Drawn, and What Is Still Unresolved</h2>

<p>The regional plan and Weber County's preserved corridor both carry SR-177 north on 5100 West to about 3000–3300 South. From there the line curves northwest across the Weber River toward 6300–6700 West, passes the west side of Plain City, and turns east to I-15 near the Box Elder County line.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-roadway-lines-2023" %}{% cite "weber-north-legacy-2009-study" %}{% cite "weber-legacy-priority-resolution-2021" %} In the WFRC 2023–2050 plan, the segment from 4000 South to 900 South is in Phase 3 (2043–2050), and the segment from 900 South to I-15 is unfunded.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-roadway-lines-2023" %}</p>

<p>That line is not a UDOT decision. At a March 3, 2026 joint meeting, a Weber County commissioner reported that UDOT Region 1 prefers an eastern alignment north of West Haven.{% cite "wc-pc-joint-minutes-mar2026" %} On June 29, 2026, the County Commission approved sending UDOT a letter asking to keep the "West Weber freeway" west of the Weber River.{% cite "wc-ws-minutes-jun2026-west-weber-freeway" %} On August 4, 2026, county planning staff presented an alternative that curves around state-owned wildlife land and wetlands.{% cite "wc-pc-ws-minutes-aug2026-freeway" %} Neither UDOT's eastern alignment nor the county's alternative has been published, so neither is drawn on the map. A public consultant web map titled "SR-177 Level 2 Screening" (August–September 2026) includes a study area labeled "SR177 Phase 4" from 4000 South to the Willard area. It is working GIS, not an announced UDOT study.{% cite "arcgis-hdr-sr177-level2-screening" %}</p>

