<div class="section-label">Geographic Scope</div>
<h2>The Phase 4 Segment: 4000 South to Box Elder County Line</h2>

<p>Phase 4 extends the SR-177 corridor from the Phase 3 terminus (4000 South in West Haven) northward approximately 10–15 miles to the Box Elder County line. The segment passes through:</p>

<ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
  <li><strong>West Haven (south end):</strong> 4000 South boundary, along the city's western edge</li>
  <li><strong>Unincorporated West-Central Weber County:</strong> Agricultural and open land in the Taylor, West Weber, Reese, and West Warren areas</li>
  <li><strong>Plain City area:</strong> West and north sides of Plain City</li>
  <li><strong>Box Elder County (north end):</strong> Connection to I-15 near the county line</li>
</ul>

<p>This list follows the preserved corridor and the regional-plan line shown on the map above.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-roadway-lines-2023" %}{% cite "weber-legacy-priority-resolution-2021" %} Hooper lies south of 4000 South, in the Phase 3 study segment. UDOT has not formally determined the alignment, cities affected, or terminus point within Box Elder County as of September 27, 2026.</p>

