<div class="section-label">Regional Context</div>
<h2>Why Box Elder Is the Terminus</h2>

<p>The designation of Box Elder County line as the Phase 4 terminus reflects regional transportation planning priorities:</p>

<ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
  <li><strong>Regional Connection:</strong> SR-177 serves the Wasatch Front (Davis/Weber) commuter corridor. Extending beyond Box Elder would reach more rural, lower-density areas with different transportation needs.</li>
  <li><strong>Funding Efficiency:</strong> Prioritizing the Davis County (completed) and Weber County (underway) segments first addresses the primary commuter demand before expanding further north.</li>
  <li><strong>Box Elder County Authority:</strong> Future Phase 4 planning would involve Box Elder County and regional coordination beyond the Wasatch Front-focused Wasatch Front Regional Council.</li>
  <li><strong>Long-Range Feasibility:</strong> Population growth projections (2043–2050) may justify further extension at that time; current justification doesn't support immediate planning.</li>
</ul>

